<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Åsa Haraldsdottir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Åsa Haraldsdottir was a Norwegian queen of the 9th century known from the sagas, a daughter of King Harald Redbeard of Agder. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri Sturluson</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heimskringla">Heimskringla</a>, King Gudrød the Hunter of Vestfold took her by force after killing her father; she later had him killed and returned to Agder with their son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halfdan-the-black">Halfdan the Black</a>, father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a>. She is often linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oseberg-ship">Oseberg ship</a> burial.</p></div>
